From: Toxblh <toxblh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: aspeed-vhub: no zero-length packets for the network functions

On the AST2500 the bulk IN endpoint of an NCM gadget stopped for good
under load with one DMA descriptor pending (the read pointer one behind
the CPU write pointer, no error anywhere). u_ether ends an IN transfer of
a multiple of the packet size with a zero-length descriptor; with the
gadget marked as not supporting ZLPs it pads the transfer by a byte
instead (allowed for NCM and ECM). Only f_ncm and f_ecm read the quirk.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/aspeed-vhub/dev.c	2026-11-05 18:56:31.675183375 +0000
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/aspeed-vhub/dev.c	2026-11-05 18:56:31.744528236 +0000
@@ -592,6 +592,14 @@
 	else
 		d->gadget.max_speed = USB_SPEED_HIGH;
 	d->gadget.speed = USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
+	/*
+	 * No zero-length packets from the network functions (u_ether: NCM,
+	 * ECM pad the transfer by a byte instead): on the AST2500 a bulk IN
+	 * endpoint in descriptor mode stopped for good with one descriptor
+	 * pending under load (REIMU: the USB network to the host, NCM; its
+	 * transfers of a multiple of 512 bytes end with a 0-length descriptor)
+	 */
+	d->gadget.quirk_zlp_not_supp = 1;
 	d->gadget.dev.of_node = vhub->pdev->dev.of_node;
 	d->gadget.dev.of_node_reused = true;
 
